FerrionOS change to the upstream bootloader (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit f3d9261b5fc81418c259c5059f46ee7087e86ed8 after the existing recipe patches.

The passphrase prompt shows the FerrionOS mark, the account names the installer wrote to EFI/BOOT/UNLOCK.TXT on the EFI system partition, and one password field. After an unlock the kernel environment carries REDOXFS_UNLOCK_SLOT (the key slot that opened the volume) and REDOXFS_UNLOCK_KIND (recovery when the typed key has the shape of a recovery key, else passphrase), written after the measured part; lines with those names typed in the environment editor are removed.

